                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 25 at 1:30AM MDT until September 25 at 7:30AM MDT by NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "description": "FFWEPZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Otero County in south central New Mexico...\n\n* Until 730 AM MDT.\n\n* At 130 AM MDT, Moderate to heavy rainfall falling over highly\nsaturated ground in the eastern Sacramento Mountains will lead to\nconsiderable flooding in area streams overnight. Impacts will be\nworse the further downstream, or east you go, as runoff builds up.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nroads, and low water crossings. Washouts and stream bank\nerosion are likely.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSacramento, Mayhill, Weed, Sixteen Springs, James Canyon, Cox\nCanyon and Hay Canyon.\n\n\n\nImpacted streams include, but are not limited to...\nRio Penasco, Agua Chiquita Creek, Bluewater Creek, Dry Burnt Canyon,\nElk Canyon, Lower Portions of Hay Canyon, Cox Canyon, and James\nCanyon.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWEPZ"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS54 KEPZ 250730"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDetection": [
                        "RADAR INDICATED"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDamageThreat": [
                        "CONSIDERABLE"
                    ],
                    "BLOCKCHANNEL": [
                        "EAS",
                        "NWEM"
                    ],
                    "EAS-ORG": [
                        "WXR"
                    ],
                    "VTEC": [
                        "/O.NEW.KEPZ.FF.W.0175.260925T0730Z-260925T1330Z/"
                    ],
                    "eventEndingTime": [
                        "2026-09-25T07:30:00-06:00"
                    ],
                    "WEAHandling": [
                        "Imminent Threat"
                    ],
                    "CMAMtext": [
                        "NWS: FLASH FLOOD WARNING this area til 7:30 AM MDT. Avoid flooded areas."
                    ],
                    "CMAMlongtext": [
                        "National Weather Service: A FLASH FLOOD WARNING is in effect for this area until 7:30 AM MDT. This is a dangerous and life-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are fleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order."
                    ]
